---
/**
 * Intro curtain.
 *
 * The mark is the centrepiece, as a real extruded solid: a GLB generated from
 * the 2D logo (Higgsfield image → render → mesh), lit and turned in a small
 * WebGL scene. It starts edge-on and rotates to face the reader while the
 * meter fills, then the curtain wipes up into the hero.
 *
 * Two marks live in here and exactly one is ever seen. The SVG is the
 * fallback: it draws itself with a real stroke-dash tween over the real path,
 * and it is what plays when WebGL is missing, the GLB is slow, or three.js
 * fails to load. The motion engine picks between them and reveals the winner —
 * neither is visible until it does, so a failure never shows two logos.
 *
 * Hidden without JavaScript (`display:none` until `html.js`), removed after
 * the first play of a session, and never shown under reduced motion.
 */
---

<div class="preloader" data-preloader aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="preloader__inner">
    <div class="preloader__stage">
      <canvas class="preloader__canvas" data-intro-canvas></canvas>

      <svg viewBox="0 0 61 87" fill="none" class="preloader__mark" data-intro-fallback>
        <g transform="translate(-69 -56)">
